Ladybird now transfers the used main size of a replaced flex item with
only a natural aspect ratio through that ratio to its cross size. Run
in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and Playwright’s WebKit 26.5,
Chrome and Firefox agree; WebKit makes an image like this without
max-width 150px in a 100px container.

Blink’s ComputeReplacedSizeInternal() derives the block size from
the flexed inline size; its stretch fallback for a box without a
natural size applies only while both sizes are unresolved. WebKit’s
RenderReplaced::computeReplacedLogicalHeight() derives the height
of a box without a natural size from its used width. And Gecko’s
nsContainerFrame::ComputeSizeWithIntrinsicDimensions() uses the
ratio-dependent size of the definite inline size, with no exception for
a box without a natural size.
